{"as_of":"2026-09-23","events":[{"date":"2025-01-01","tag":"gas","title":"Russian gas transit through Ukraine ends","body":"The Gazprom–Naftogaz transit contract expired. It had carried about half of Russia's remaining pipeline gas to the EU; TurkStream is now the only direct route.","sources":[{"label":"CNN, 1 Jan 2025: Ukraine ends Russian gas transit","url":"https://edition.cnn.com/2025/01/01/business/ukraine-russia-gas-eu-halted-hnk-intl"}]},{"date":"2025-09-27","tag":"oil","title":"Kirkuk–Ceyhan pipeline restarts","body":"Iraqi Kurdistan crude resumed flowing to Türkiye's Ceyhan terminal at about 0.24 mb/d after a 2½-year halt.","sources":[{"label":"Al Jazeera, 27 Sep 2025: Iraq resumes Kurdish oil exports to Türkiye","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/9/27/iraq-resumes-kurdish-oil-exports-to-turkiye-after-two-and-a-half-year-halt"}]},{"date":"2025-10-22","tag":"sanctions","title":"US sanctions Rosneft and Lukoil","body":"OFAC blocked Russia's two largest oil producers, which account for about 55% of Russian output. The UK and EU took parallel measures.","sources":[{"label":"Sullivan & Cromwell: US sanctions Rosneft and Lukoil (22 Oct 2025)","url":"https://www.sullcrom.com/insights/memo/2025/October/United-States-Sanctions-Significant-Russian-Oil-Companies-Rosneft-Lukoil"}]},{"date":"2026-02-28","tag":"conflict","title":"US–Israeli strikes on Iran; Hormuz closed","body":"The Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) warned that no ship may pass the Strait of Hormuz, and commercial traffic collapsed within days.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: 2026 Strait of Hormuz campaign","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Strait_of_Hormuz_campaign"}]},{"date":"2026-03-02","tag":"lng","title":"Qatar halts LNG production","body":"QatarEnergy shut Ras Laffan (~77 Mtpa, about 20% of world LNG) after Iranian strikes. The TTF gas benchmark rose more than 25% intraday and Asian JKM about 39%.","sources":[{"label":"RTÉ, 4 Mar 2026: Qatar shuts gas liquefaction","url":"https://www.rte.ie/news/business/2026/0304/1561653-qatar-shutdown/"},{"label":"Wikipedia: 2026 Iran war fuel crisis","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Iran_war_fuel_crisis"}]},{"date":"2026-03-18","tag":"lng","title":"Missiles damage Ras Laffan trains","body":"Two LNG trains (12.8 Mtpa, ~17% of Qatar's capacity) were damaged; QatarEnergy estimates repairs will take years.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: 2026 Iran war fuel crisis","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Iran_war_fuel_crisis"}]},{"date":"2026-03-28","tag":"oil","title":"Saudi East–West pipeline at a record 7 mb/d","body":"Aramco maxed out the Petroline to Yanbu on the Red Sea; crude loadings there reached about 5 mb/d.","sources":[{"label":"Fortune, 28 Mar 2026: Saudi pipeline hits 7 mb/d","url":"https://fortune.com/2026/03/28/saudi-arabia-east-west-oil-pipeline-strait-hormuz-bypass-7-million-barrels-yanbu-red-sea/"}]},{"date":"2026-04-13","tag":"conflict","title":"US naval blockade of Iranian ports","body":"The blockade followed the failure of the Islamabad talks and was confirmed on 15 April.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: 2026 Strait of Hormuz campaign","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Strait_of_Hormuz_campaign"}]},{"date":"2026-04-28","tag":"opec","title":"UAE announces exit from OPEC and OPEC+","body":"The exit took effect on 1 May 2026, ending 59 years of membership.","sources":[{"label":"CNBC, 28 Apr 2026: UAE to leave OPEC","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/04/28/uae-opec-oil-iran.html"},{"label":"EIA Today in Energy: UAE exit from OPEC+","url":"https://www.eia.gov/todayinenergy/detail.php?id=67804"}]},{"date":"2026-04-30","tag":"price","title":"Brent touches $126","body":"An intraday four-year high, reached after threats of a wider blockade.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: 2026–2028 world oil market chronology","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026%E2%80%932028_world_oil_market_chronology"}]},{"date":"2026-06-09","tag":"oil","title":"Middle East output down by more than 11 mb/d","body":"EIA estimated that OECD inventories would fall to their lowest level since 2003.","sources":[{"label":"EIA press release, 9 Jun 2026","url":"https://www.eia.gov/pressroom/releases/press589.php"}]},{"date":"2026-06-17","tag":"conflict","title":"US–Iran memorandum signed","body":"Tankers briefly transited Hormuz and Brent fell to $73.74 by 24 June.","sources":[{"label":"Al Jazeera, 9 Jul 2026: what happened since the US–Iran MoU","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/7/9/strait-of-hormuz-what-has-happened-since-the-us-iran-mou-on-june-17"},{"label":"Wikipedia: 2026–2028 world oil market chronology","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026%E2%80%932028_world_oil_market_chronology"}]},{"date":"2026-07-08","tag":"conflict","title":"Truce collapses; blockade reinstated","body":"Attacks on commercial ships ended the interim ceasefire, and the US reimposed its blockade on 14–15 July.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: 2026 Strait of Hormuz campaign","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Strait_of_Hormuz_campaign"},{"label":"Al Jazeera, 9 Jul 2026: what happened since the US–Iran MoU","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/7/9/strait-of-hormuz-what-has-happened-since-the-us-iran-mou-on-june-17"}]},{"date":"2026-08-25","tag":"conflict","title":"More than 100 mines cleared from Hormuz lanes","body":"The US Navy and contractors reported clearing the traffic separation scheme, though transits stayed near zero.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: 2026 Strait of Hormuz campaign","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Strait_of_Hormuz_campaign"}]},{"date":"2026-09-08","tag":"lng","title":"Qatar: 18 LNG cargoes in six months","body":"That compares with 509 in the same period a year earlier. Non-Gulf supply offset about 75% of the loss.","sources":[{"label":"Euronews, 8 Sep 2026: Qatar and UAE test ways to keep LNG moving","url":"https://www.euronews.com/business/2026/09/08/six-months-into-hormuz-blockade-qatar-and-uae-test-ways-to-keep-lng-moving"}]